<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Judith of France</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 843–<a href="/years/870">870</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Judith, Queen of Wessex</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Judith was a daughter of the Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> who married two kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>, Æthelwulf in 856 and then his son Æthelbald. Widowed, she eloped in 862 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-of-flanders">Baldwin Iron Arm</a>, and after her father reluctantly accepted the marriage Baldwin received lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a>, the core of the later County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>. Their son Baldwin II married Ælfthryth, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a>.</p></div>
